# Rank 1595 / CVE-2023-44270: PostCSS's tokenizer recognised every
# line terminator except a bare carriage return in its bad-bracket
# pattern, so input using \r line endings kept an unclosed bracket
# token open across lines and confused every tool relying on
# PostCSS's token positions (incorrect parsing enabling downstream
# bypasses, CWE-74/CWE-1284 family; the advisory notes security
# tools that sanitize CSS through PostCSS). RE_BAD_BRACKET in
# lib/tokenize.js read `/.[\n"'(/\\]/` -- \n but not \r -- while
# RE_AT_END and RE_WORD_END carry both. The fixing commit 58cc860b4c
# ("Fix carrier return parsing"): the
# class gains \r, `/.[\r\n"'(/\\]/`, with parse tests for
# \r-terminated input. .
#
# ATTENTION, terminator-class completeness. The parser exists and
# its terminator handling is mostly right -- one character class
# omitted a terminator the CSS grammar defines, the same
# grammar-completeness family as rank 1573 (single-quote encoding
# declarations): no rule can ask "does every character class that
# enumerates line terminators include all of them" -- class
# completeness against a grammar is enumeration vocabulary. A
# binding on PostCSS's own tokenizer would detect this library
# rather than the weakness. Measured on the real code: scanning
# lib/tokenize.js reports zero findings at both revisions. No
# ENGINE-GAPS.md entry. No definition change shipped. Spec
# cve_rank1595 records the \n-only bad-bracket class and the
# \r\n-complete form, both asserting reject VYQL-VAL-016: when
# grammar-completeness vocabulary lands, the incomplete class must
# flip to expect.

test "rank1595: the bad bracket class omits the carriage return"
  lang javascript
  file lib/tokenize.js
  reject VYQL-VAL-016
  code
  ```
  const RE_NEWLINE = /\r?\n|\r/;
  const RE_BAD_BRACKET = /.[\n"'(/\\]/;

  function tokenizer(input) {
      const tokens = [];
      let pos = 0;
      while (pos < input.length) {
          const code = input.charCodeAt(pos);
          if (code === 40) {
              const match = input.slice(pos).match(RE_BAD_BRACKET);
              if (match === null) {
                  pos++;
                  continue;
              }
              const end = pos + match.index + 1;
              tokens.push(['bracket', input.slice(pos, end)]);
              pos = end;
          } else {
              pos++;
          }
      }
      return tokens;
  }
  ```

test "rank1595: the fixed revision includes every line terminator"
  lang javascript
  file lib/tokenize.js
  reject VYQL-VAL-016
  code
  ```
  const RE_NEWLINE = /\r?\n|\r/;
  const RE_BAD_BRACKET = /.[\r\n"'(/\\]/;

  function tokenizer(input) {
      const tokens = [];
      let pos = 0;
      while (pos < input.length) {
          const code = input.charCodeAt(pos);
          if (code === 40) {
              const match = input.slice(pos).match(RE_BAD_BRACKET);
              if (match === null) {
                  pos++;
                  continue;
              }
              const end = pos + match.index + 1;
              tokens.push(['bracket', input.slice(pos, end)]);
              pos = end;
          } else {
              pos++;
          }
      }
      return tokens;
  }
  ```
